 ## Background
-Fast Volume Reconstruction was introduced in the context of Discretized Gaussian Representation (DGR) for tomographic reconstruction [S2]. It addresses the limitations of 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) when applied to CT, specifically integration bias and density inconsistency [S1, unofficial]. The method was developed to enable efficient, differentiable volume rendering for 3D tomography, allowing for joint optimization of Gaussian parameters [S2]. It is used in public CT datasets such as FIPS, AAPM-Mayo LDCT, and FUMPE [S2].
